#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0530 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "NEW with the M2-P9 ruling (option (b) / M2-D29, Fix #307), and the FIRST fixture this rule has ever carried. CDISC-CG0530 was already narrowed to ['SCREEN FAILURE', 'NOT ASSIGNED'] - the finding's claim that it 'travels with' PMDA-SD1366 had nothing to do - so the only thing that moved here is the fifth ARMNULRS term (SDTM CT C142179, added 2025-09-26). Row 1 fires; row 2 is the conformant control on the same term; row 3 is the boundary the narrowing exists for ('ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED' WAS randomised, so rows 1167-1172's Cited Guidance keeps RFENDTC populated and the rule must stay silent)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 RFENDTC=2020-02-10
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFSTDTC  type=Char label="Subject Reference Start Date/Time"
col RFENDTC  type=Char label="Subject Reference End Date/Time"
col ARMNRS   type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 |            | 2020-02-10 | SCREENING NOT COMPLETED
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1023 |            |            | SCREENING NOT COMPLETED
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1034 | 2020-01-05 | 2020-02-10 | ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED
